[[15,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/2429529\">7015A04</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429358\">5050C34</a></p><p>1. Disconnect the motor electrical connection.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001294.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Connector</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Rear window wiper motor</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p><a href=\"#/2428667\">N16</a></p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Undo the bolts.</p><p>3. Remove the motor.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2044995.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[15,1,0,"<p>1. Working from the outside of the rear widow, remove the gasket\non the  hole thorugh the glass and check it is undamaged.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2044996.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[15,1,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Check that the rear wiper motor\nis undamaged and operating correctly.</p><p>Position the motor and secure with bolts.</p><p>Connect the electrical connection.</p><p><a href=\"#/2429358\">5050C34</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2429529\">7015A04</a></p><p>Check that the wiper is operating efficiently.</p>"]]